        "text": "A full node is the best way to get an accurate image of the blockchain. Without one, you need to trust a third party to feed you the data you need, but because they download, validate and store all of that information they might not appeal to everyone. The Bitcoin blockchain is over 400 gigabytes as of mid 2022. Nodes download and validate blocks at 10 minute intervals. To some this may be a strain on storage and bandwidth. On the other hand, light nodes are devices that connect to other nodes but perform limited validation on the data. Because of this they have lower storage and bandwidth requirements and can be run on devices such as cell phones or low end computers. If you use a non custodial wallet that's most likely a light node. Instead of downloading full blocks, light nodes download only the block headers which are much smaller in size. The block header gives you important information such as previous block hash, timestamp and other metadata.",
        "start": 560,
        "end": 56700,
        "confidence": 0.98768973,
